silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_yoneda_hom_leg a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementYonedaHomLegExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'YonedaLemmaStatementYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In 'Yoneda Lemma Statement', the bijection phi maps each natural transformation tau from the representable profile to ClinicalLabels to the clinical label phi(tau) = tau_{Mittens}(id_{Mittens}) at the apex; monic because different natural transformations map to different apex elements by the bijection.; also, In 'Yoneda Lemma Statement', the inverse psi maps each clinical label x at MittensColimitApex to a natural transformation psi_x; monic because different labels produce different natural transformations (injectivity of psi follows from injectivity of phi)." .
